# The IPC benchmark's medians (user/ipcbench, CPU cycles by its ruler) as
# measured on 2026-10-15 on the P53's Intel Core i7-9850H, through KVM in
# QEMU 10.0.13 inside the build VM (8 vCPUs), with nothing else running there:
# 10 runs of the bench-gate entry of test/selftest.sh, on the kernel with the
# run queues (Phase 3 step 10). Their ranges: 492-496, 1548, 1088-1092.
# Earlier: 2026-10-14, 384, 1344, 880 (the system call's figure from the old
# clock-cost method, too low in most runs; the run queues not yet built);
# 2026-10-13 on the Intel Core i5-14400: 376, 1356, 764.
# Why these moved (docs/phase3-data/README.md, *Step 10*): ipcbench now takes
# off the clock's real cost (+90 or so on the system call), and the run queues
# cost 172 cycles a round trip and 24 a system call (choice 9).
# The gate in test/selftest.sh fails a run whose median is more than 25% above
# these (docs/phase3-plan.md, *Testing*). Change them only with a measurement
# and a reason, recorded in docs/phase3-data.
#
# measurement (the start of the line ipcbench prints) | median
a system call that does nothing|496
two address spaces, passive server|1548
one address space, passive server|1092
